WEBVTT

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.010
Anne.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.060
Yes, Matthew?

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.670
Well... you haven't forgotten something, have you?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.680
No, it's all right. I managed to
get everything ready yesterday.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.540
I see.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:29.880
What's wrong, Matthew?

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:32.580
Oh, it's nothing.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.550
Well... will you come back to
Avonlea during your holidays?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.090
Of course! Have you been worried
about that, Matthew?

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:46.010
No, that's... I mean...

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.600
No. You're right.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.610
Driving this carriage with you beside me,

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.410
I remember the day when
you came to Green Gables.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:04.330
Matthew, do you want ice-cream
when we reach Charlottetown?

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.440
It's very delicious.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:14.100
Really? I haven't eaten any in years.
Perhaps I should try one?

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.360
Yes!

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.060
Let's go!

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:37.580
Here.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.220
Well?

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.540
It's quite good.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.330
Isn't it?

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.230
Anne, you're finally here.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:38.140
I thought you would arrive a while ago.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.990
Welcome, Mr. Matthew Cuthbert.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.490
Thank you, this time...

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.230
We're very much indebted...

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:50.170
Now, now. Come in and take a rest.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.000
You're both tired, aren't you?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.740
As I wrote in the letter,

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:01.110
the lady who owns the boarding house
has a high social status.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.980
Her husband used to be a British officer,

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.220
and she's very careful when
deciding who can board.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.200
You don't have to worry about
meeting any objectionable persons there.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:20.660
Initially, I really wanted you to stay at my house.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:25.010
But it would be too far to go
there and back every day, right?

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:31.110
But the surroundings are quiet,
and the food's not bad. I like it, too.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:34.910
If you don't eat well,
your studies will be affected.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:48.360
Well, we've arrived.
That's your room, Anne.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:57.030
You're Mr. Matthew Cuthbert, I presume?

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.410
Welcome.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.360
I'm indebted to you.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:04.040
I'm Anne Shirley. Pleased to meet you.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:08.580
And to you. You seem like a good girl.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:12.040
Miss Barry was saying that you were
number one in the entrance exam.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:17.130
Needless to say, it is the very
duty of all students to work hard.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.720
You must continue to work hard.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.770
I would like you to become
a model for other students.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.570
Y-Yes, that's what I intend to do.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.030
Well, excuse me.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.110
I'll take care of everyday things.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:33.550
Now, let me show you to your room.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:01.130
Now that Anne is no longer around, Marilla cannot sit still.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.440
She can only work diligently
to forget her loneliness.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:10.340
In order to hold back the urge to cry,

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:13.230
she plunges fiercely into unnecessary work.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.350
She works the whole day long.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.130
Who's that?

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.980
Oh, this? This is Miss Stacy.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.740
Oh! Was she the one who led
the exercises during the exams?

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:20.630
Yes.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:24.350
It's all thanks to Miss Stacy that
I can study at Queen's.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.280
She's like my guardian angel.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:29.350
Well, well. Your guardian angel?

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:33.490
These curtains aren't bad,
the bed is good, too.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.720
And the luggage has been unpacked.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:39.350
Well, it looks like everything is ready, Anne.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:42.110
Eh? Yes! Thank you so much.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.230
Well, perhaps we'd better return to Beechwood?

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.020
R-Right.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:50.600
Matthew.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.910
It's too early to bid farewell.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.320
I'd like you two to stay at my place tonight.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.380
Don't worry.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:06.590
Thinking Anne would feel lonely,
I already informed the people here.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.310
I've arranged for a carriage to take you
to the Academy tomorrow morning,

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.120
so you don't have to worry.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.600
Then I'll let Anne do that.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.130
Well... I've decided to go home now, Anne.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:25.340
Oh, you shouldn't do that.
It's almost evening, isn't it?

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:30.280
Well, that... There's a harvest tomorrow.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:34.860
Well, I should hurry back so that
Marilla won't be worried.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.050
I see. What a pity.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.860
Anyway, Anne, you will come, won't you?

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:57.110
After bidding Anne farewell
at Miss Barry's house,

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.910
Matthew drives the carriage alone,

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:03.400
and reaches Green Gables
late in the night.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:11.470
Marilla feels that Matthew
doesn't only look tired.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.930
He looks as though there
is something missing in his heart,

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.090
and he is overcome with loneliness.

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:26.430
Did you thank Miss Josephine Barry
properly, Matthew?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:31.010
Yes, I thanked her several times, Marilla.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:32.900
Thank you for that.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.110
Yes.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.490
The tea's getting cold.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:47.700
I don't want it.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.980
You must be exhausted, brother.

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:55.220
But the harvest has been
delayed for some time.

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.270
You'd better go to bed early.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.440
You're right.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.740
That night, Marilla cries
for the very first time.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.550
Knowing that the figure of her
lively, young girl is no longer there

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:46.710
in the gable room at the end of the hall,

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.160
and thinking she won't be hearing her soft breathing again,

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:54.060
Marilla is filled with heart ache.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.690
Thank you, Miss Josephine Barry.
I'm going in now.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:17.750
Work hard now. Visit me when you have time.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.450
I will!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.530
Anne! Anne!

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.170
Good morning, Anne!

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.270
Good morning.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.970
The classes will be formed today, right?

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:44.410
Anne, you will enter the advanced level class, right?

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:47.440
Yes. If I pass the final exam,

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:50.370
I can get a First Class teacher's license in one year.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:52.980
Miss Stacy advised me to do so.

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.920
That's because you are a prodigy.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.550
We've all chosen the 2nd grade
class as it'll be more relaxing.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:03.030
After all, you only need a 2nd class
license to become a teacher.

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:06.500
It's a pity we can't be in the
same class as you, Anne.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.270
In the end, only you and Gilbert opted for First Class.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:10.840
Yes.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.240
Anne and Gilbert don't seem
to get along well.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.580
But you'll soon make friends.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:18.260
Oh my! Josie already found one.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.830
Good morning! They are friends from Avonlea.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:24.970
This is Frank Stockley. We're staying
at the same boarding house.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.840
We're already good friends.
Am I right, Frank?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:35.850
All of you made it to the Queen's
with remarkable results.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:40.840
Among the first class of fifty,
Anne only recognizes

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:47.320
the tall brown-haired boy
sitting across the classroom.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.850
Also, due to the present circumstances,

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:53.690
it does not seem to help very much,
even though they are acquainted.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.310
Anne feels depressed.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:58.450
I do wish Jane and Ruby
had opted for First Class, too.

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:04.410
As you know, the duty as a student of Queen's Academy...

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:07.400
But if I could find a friend here,

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.350
the feeling I'm having now, like a
cat that's lost in a strange attic,

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.970
would certainly go away.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.840
I wonder who I can make friends with.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.880
But just as I had promised Diana,

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:25.620
no matter how many friends I get
to know at the Queen's,

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.260
no one will be as dear to me as she is.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:32.100
Still, there are many here that
I could make friends with.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.170
That girl should be fine.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.650
She looks lively and rosy.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:42.340
The blonde girl across at
the back seems fine, too.

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:45.840
She has been looking out of the window
since the teacher started speaking

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.640
as if she's in a sweet dream.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:56.090
But they don't know me. Maybe they
don't want to be my friends at all.

00:14:56.130 --> 00:15:00.330
Students in the first class must
not rely on luck in your studies.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:04.390
You have to complete two
years' work within one year,

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:07.050
so you have to prepare
yourselves appropriately.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:11.050
But your efforts will be rewarded.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.870
Especially when the graduation
gold medal of highest honor

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:19.980
will be shining brilliantly on the
chest of one of you fifty students.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:25.070
Gilbert's has that glint in his eyes.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:28.950
I'm sure he wants to receive the medal.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:33.860
Everyone, don't wait till tomorrow.
Start to work hard today.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:39.940
All of a sudden, Anne recalls her
fighting spirit in the past.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:43.340
She will continue to compete with
Gilbert Blythe in the days to come.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.840
This can be her pillar of strength.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.670
Even if they don't get to be friends,

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:50.550
it's fortunate that they
are still in the same class.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:53.830
That's what Anne begins to think.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:21.790
I'm back.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.520
It's Anne Shirley.

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:26.840
Welcome back. You must be tired
from your first day of school.

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:30.410
Dinner will be served at 7 pm.
Please be punctual.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.780
Yes. I understand.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:41.390
The first day in school has passed
in a vortex of excitement and curiosity,

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.880
but it has been quite interesting.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:49.230
That night, at twilight, when Anne finds
herself alone in her room in the boarding house,

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.080
feelings of loneliness well up.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.680
I'm back, Miss Stacy.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.760
Diana...

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:06.850
No matter what happens,
I won't cry, as it's weak and silly.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.180
Marilla.

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:29.680
It's not working.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.680
I have to think of something
funny to stop my tears.

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:45.550
But everything funny is
related to Avonlea.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.880
The more I recall, the sadder I get.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:54.220
I'll be able to go home next Friday.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.680
But that seems like hundreds of years away.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:04.120
I can't cheer up. I don't want to cheer up!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.260
It's better to be miserable!

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.890
Y-Yes! Please come in.

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:20.170
Oh my, Josie! Are you here to visit me?

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.820
You've been crying, haven't you? Are you homesick?

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:28.080
I guess.

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:31.480
Some people have so little
self-control in that respect.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.320
I've no intention of being
homesick, I can tell you.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:39.270
Compared to a place like Avonlea,
this city is much more interesting.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:44.160
I wonder how I could
stay there for so long.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:47.330
You shouldn't cry, Anne.
It isn't becoming.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:53.170
Because your nose and eyes get red,
and then you seem ALL red.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.640
I had a great time at the Academy today.

00:19:55.680 --> 00:20:00.140
Our French professor is simply adorable.
He has a lovely mustache.

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:05.280
Anne, do you have something to eat around?
I'm literally starving.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.570
Oh my! I thought so!

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:09.290
I'll help myself.

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:13.920
I was sure Marilla would've packed
a lot of snacks for you.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.330
That's why I called round.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:21.360
Otherwise I'd have gone to the park
with Frank Stockley to hear the band play.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:26.180
Frank is the boy I introduced this
morning. He's quite interesting.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:30.380
He even asked who
that red-haired girl was.

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:34.510
I told him you were an orphan
that the Cuthberts had adopted,

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:37.100
and nobody knew very much
about what you'd been before that.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.340
Josie Pye!

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:41.920
Oh! It's delicious. Can I have one more?

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:43.690
It's us, Anne. Are you in?

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:45.190
Ruby! Jane!

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:49.260
Anne! It feels like it's already been a few
months since we parted this morning.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:51.010
How true! You really came!

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.500
Oh, so Josie came here, too.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.890
Josie and Jane are not talking to each other today.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:01.870
Actually, I'm supposed to stay in
my room to study Latin.

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:07.210
That's true! That horrid old professor gave
us twenty lines to study on the first day.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:11.650
But I just can't settle down to study tonight.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:12.780
Right.

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:17.470
Hey, those are traces of tears.
You cried, too, didn't you, Anne?

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:21.440
If you've been crying, please admit it.
It will make me feel better,

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:24.730
because I was crying really hard
before Ruby came along.

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:26.090
So were you, right?

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:27.510
Y-Yes.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:33.270
Oh, that's great! I don't mind being a goose
so much if somebody else is goosey, too.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:34.030
Right, Ruby?

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.430
Yes.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:41.810
Ah, wait a moment.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:45.310
Please have some.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:46.620
Oh my! Cookies!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.090
Marilla made them.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:49.190
Let me try one.

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:50.650
Me, too.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:54.090
It has the real Avonlea flavor, doesn't it?

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:58.230
Anne, you mean to try for the gold medal, don't you?

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:00.310
Yes.

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:03.990
After all, there's nothing wrong in having big dreams.

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.520
Of course not. You can definitely do it, Anne.

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.070
But there's Gilbert as well.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:09.440
That's fine.

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:11.860
Oh, that reminds me.

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:17.810
In future, Queen's students can also
apply for the Avery scholarship.

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:19.230
My! The Avery scholarship?

00:22:19.490 --> 00:22:23.890
That's what Frank said. His uncle is one
of the board of governors, you see.

00:22:23.930 --> 00:22:27.020
I heard it'll be officially announced
in school tomorrow.

00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:28.530
What is the Avery scholarship?

00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:31.190
Oh my! Don't you know?

00:22:31.230 --> 00:22:37.900
It's awarded to the student with the
highest mark in English and English Literature.

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:44.090
Right! The scholarship is $250 a year. Enough to
pay four years' fees at Redmond College.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:45.800
Redmond College?

00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:46.750
Yes.

00:22:46.780 --> 00:22:51.650
The scholarship was a part of the inheritance of
a wealthy person of New Brunswick.

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:54.050
Redmond College...

00:22:57.390 --> 00:22:59.290
Anne feels her heart beat more quickly,

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:03.190
and the horizons of her ambition shift and broaden.

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:05.170
Anne's highest pinnacle of
aspiration has been

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:08.550
a teacher's provincial license, First Class,
at the end of the year,

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:11.100
and perhaps the gold medal.

00:23:12.070 --> 00:23:17.030
But from this moment,
her goal has changed.

00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:21.570
If possible, I'd like to win that scholarship.

00:23:21.620 --> 00:23:24.350
English has always been my best subject.

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:30.050
If I can study at Redmond College
and obtain a Bachelor's degree,

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:32.700
I'm sure Matthew will be proud.

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:36.120
It will be hard to be
away from home for four years,

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:38.950
but I'm sure Marilla will forgive me.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:52.410
Oh, it's delightful to have ambitions!

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:57.080
Just as soon as you attain to one ambition,
you see another one glittering higher up still.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:23:59.450
Oh!

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:04.150
Having ambitions does make life so interesting.

00:24:19.040 --> 00:24:21.440
Anne comes home once a week.

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:25.370
It is a joyous occasion for Matthew and Marilla.

00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:28.790
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 43

00:24:28.910 --> 00:24:30.470
Home for the Weekends

00:24:30.510 --> 00:24:31.740
Please look forward to it!
